# armour/shared/pauldron_fur4_r: the small leather shoulder pad on the right shoulder (fur.4; LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.6,
# (FORGE-MANTLE) fur.4: its base views repeat fur.2's small leather pad, so a 0-forge leather or padded look at pauldron dial 4 draws what it drew before; the fur MANTLE is the forge styles' replace views.
# 27.2: T2's "small shoulder pads"): a boiled-leather cap 1 px past the shoulder line, matte, one step-4 shine on the lit
# top-left, no glint; `when furtrim` lays a fur edge along its rim (the Fjordfolk and Highland trim).
# Finish regions: R the rim, P the cap's face, W a spot on the shadow side. Shared by both bodies. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
role pauldron fur.4
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R
# (FORGE-MANTLE, round 2) `when shoulder-fur replace` views: the fur MANTLE drawn for the forge styles (STYLE_P2 28.3; generated by FORGE-MANTLE gen.py from shapes5.py); 0-forge looks keep the base views.

